# Pillar fields for testing which tank sizes rest on a hex grid of thin
# pillars. A tank rests on an obstacle while any part of its box is over
# one, so the spacing decides who falls between them.
#
# West field, spacing 8.5: a normal tank (6 x 2.8) can sit wholly in a gap
# and drops; an Obese one (15 x 7) always spans a pillar.
# East field, spacing 3.75: a normal tank always spans a pillar; a Tiny
# one (2.4 x 1.12) can drop between them.
#
# Pillars are 1 x 1 and 1.5 tall; jump onto the step at the south edge of
# each field, then drive onto the pillars. Obese flags sit beside the west
# step, Tiny flags beside the east one.

metadata
  title Pillar test
  author Tim Riker <timriker@gmail.com>
  license AGPL-3.0-only
  description Hex pillar fields that hold Obese but not normal tanks, and normal but not Tiny ones.
endmetadata

world
  name Pillar test
  size 100
end

options
  -j
  -setforced _jumpFlagVelocity _jumpVelocity*1.414
  -srvmsg "West field: Obese stays up, normal falls. East field: normal stays up, Tiny falls."
end

box
  name obese_0_0
  position -75.000 -20.000 0
  size 0.5 0.5 1.5
  rotation 0
end

